Z||000000||Wolfhound||01-04-2000||11:13 AM||||My air conditioning belt is missing. the crank pully and compressor pully have  flat teeth that the belt runs on. The parts houses have listings only for a standard V-belt. Anyone know the proper belt for this compressor. Is it maybe a change that occured during the year? The car is an 87 GT.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 01-04-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Dave85||01-04-2000||04:20 PM||||My compressor belt was a regular V belt. '85 GT. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||01-04-2000||04:23 PM||||My 88 Formula has a regular old fashioned V belt on the AC compressor. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave85||01-04-2000||04:26 PM||||Just another thought, The belt missing could be an indication of a bad compressor. That seems to be a very common problem.  Mine had/has a bad compressor and once it started getting noisy off came the belt. Problem solved (untill summer)!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||01-04-2000||09:14 PM||||I have to at least put a belt on to see if The thing works. It,s a flat toothed belt. It was 77 degrees here yesterday in L.A.(Lower Alabama). Made me think about it. It spins free and lock when I turn on the AC. Has no one on the forum seen this belt? My options sticker has the code for A.C <BR> I guess I could pull a mold off the pully and take a measurement.<P> Might be something minor, might not.<P> There is no way this is a V-belt. Looks like  the timeing belt pully belt on a honda.  quarter inch deep, maybe five eigths wide. Yeah it,s probably broke but I gotta start some where.<BR>Coy<P>||||reg||7
Z||000005||fiero56||01-04-2000||10:19 PM||||My formula has A/C, and it just has a regular v-belt. I know the A/C is stock since the window sticker shows it. The a/c pulley on mine is not flat, it is shaped for a v-belt. I do remember reading in my Haynes that there were several a/c compressors used on the Fiero. I'd have to check to see if it mentions alterante belts.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||01-05-2000||07:48 AM||||My 85SE v-6 has the standard V-belt.  I just replaced the A/C compressor, accumulator, flushed the system and replaced every o-ring in the system, and converted to R-134.  It pulled vacuum fine and seems to be working fine so far.<P>Fieros used two different compressors.  Mine uses a DA-6.  The parts book lists two different size pulleys for this also.<P>You might try calling Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory at (256) 420-5391.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll  ||||reg||1
